From df0efa5108b72919153d58cbd5d3d0bf033ae92b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Needham <06needhamt@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:56:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] access: add HD DVD module using libhddvd

An access-demux for HD DVD discs, in the manner of the Blu-ray module.
libhddvd lists the disc's titles and chapters and reads a title's EVO
sectors as one MPEG program stream, which a chained PS demuxer parses.

Standard Content discs play as authored: first play, menus that jump and
the links between cells are followed through libhddvd's navigator, which
also takes the user's title, chapter and menu choices and seeks.

The experimental hddvd-guess option (off by default) turns on libhddvd's
guesses at the parts of Standard Content navigation whose HD DVD layout is
not known, read as DVD-Video lays them out: menu and first-play cells
play, with their stills; VLC's navigation keys move between their buttons
and activate them, and the mouse selects and activates the button under
it; angle blocks play one angle; and PGC links are followed. None of these
layouts has been confirmed on a disc. A menu cell has no length and
cannot be sought in, and button highlights are not drawn.

On Advanced Content discs the playlist's titles are offered, and the
title's HDi application runs in a libhddvd menu session: its display list
is drawn as an overlay on the video, and VLC's navigation keys and the
mouse are sent to it (mouse positions are mapped through the size of the
video under the overlay, which its updater reports). Its player commands
are carried out: title and chapter jumps; pause, which stops reading until
it plays again; audio and subtitle choices by track number or language,
whose playlist streamNumber names the EVO substream (the PS demuxer gives
streams their stream ids for this); subtitle visibility; and the z-order
of its application. Starting or stopping other applications is refused,
as one application runs per title. hddvd-menu turns both kinds of menu
off.

AACS-protected titles are reported in an error dialog: libhddvd does not
decrypt.
